<p>   (benefit)		     10,810	  (6,759)     14,595</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>   extraordinary item	  13,758	 (27,633)     18,611</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss on early</p>
<p>   extinguishment of debt	  --	    (682)	   --</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	     13,758	 (28,315)     18,611</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>     extraordinary item	  1.32	   (2.44)	 1.64</p>
<p>   Extraordinary loss		--	   (0.06)	   --</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)	     1.32	   (2.50)	 l.64</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>   shares		   10,415,047     11,333,453  11,333,453</p>
<p>Note: &quot;Analytical Results&quot; depict the company's results excluding (i) the impact of business integration and other non-recurring charges, (ii) the impact of the extraordinary loss and (iii) the impact of the Pearle, Inc. and Sears Optical of Canada acquisitions in November, 1996 on the Company's operations, interest expense and per share earnings for the fiscal year ended February 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Q4 results include a $64.4 million non-recurring pretax charge ($44.4 million after tax), which places results for the year at a per share loss of $2.44 before a $.06 per share extraordinary loss associated with the extinguishment of debt. This charge was primarily related to the acquisition of Pearle and included costs incurred in connection with the integration and consolidation of Pearle into Cole, as well as other non-recurring charges.</p>
<p>Full name Cole National Corp.</p>
